        <name>sanitizeRequestedHeaders</name>
        <qualifiedname>CorsTokens::sanitizeRequestedHeaders</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>std::string_view</type>
          <declname>requested</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Filters a client-supplied Access-Control-Request-Headers value down to syntactically valid tokens. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Rejects the whole value when it is empty or longer than 1024 characters, then keeps only comma-separated tokens made entirely of token characters and rejoins them with &quot;, &quot;. This prevents a preflight request from echoing CRLF, quotes or arbitrary separators into Access-Control-Allow-Headers. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">requested</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Raw header value from the request. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A comma-and-space separated list of safe tokens, or an empty string when nothing is acceptable. An empty result tells <ref refid="namespaceCors_1a8bdb2553f14222ee4cacfb5628907590" kindref="member">Cors::apply()</ref> to fall back to the default header list. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
