        <briefdescription>
<para>Merges a token into an existing Vary header value, avoiding duplicates. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Tokens are compared case-insensitively. A &quot;*&quot; wildcard in the existing value means every response is already variable, so the value is returned unchanged; likewise when the token is already present. Otherwise the token is appended. The original string is returned unchanged when no edit is needed, which lets the caller skip the header write. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">existing</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Current Vary header value. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">value</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Token to add. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The merged Vary value. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
